   m_aBriefings {
    GC_Briefing "{3E5534F0D399CD40}" {
     m_iOrder 0
     m_sTitle "I. Situation:"
     m_sContent "<h2>I. Situation:</h2>"\
     "<b>Time & Weather:</b>"\
     "Time - 05:15"\
     "Weather - Cloudy, Some Fog"\
     ""\
     "<b>Situation:</b>"\
     "CAF secured the island of Skalisty in the early beginnings of the liberation of this region.. however the Soviets are sending in their VDV to reclaim this vital island."\
     ""\
     ""\
     "GM Note - Recommended the FLIGHT LEAD knows how to LAND NAV, It be Foggy."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF" "USSR"
     }
     m_eAudience 1
    }
    GC_Briefing "{50109EC4AD891682}" {
     m_iOrder 1
     m_sTitle "A. Enemy Forces:"
     m_sContent "<h2>A. Enemy Forces:</h2>"\
     "<b>Equipment:</b>"\
     "USSR are equipped with their standard WARSAW Pact weaponry, AK series, RPG7s, RPKs."\
     "Wearing the standard USSR uniform of VDV Camo with greenish helmet."\
     ""\
     "<b>Known Strength:</b>"\
     "1x VDV Company (-)"\
     "2x Mi-24s"\
     "4x Mi-8s"\
     ""\
     "<b>Location: </b>"\
     "At the airfield"\
     ""\
     "<b>Capabilities:</b>"\
     "Access to RPKs, RPGs."\
     "Vehicles include Mi-8s & Mi-24s"\
     ""\
     "<b>MLCOA:</b>"\
     "Land and secure the Western/Northern HQ before pushing in to secure our main HQ/Compound"\
     ""\
     "<b>MDCOA:</b>"\
     "Land and secure the Western/Northern HQ, utilizing the Mi-24 to sweep the forests with rockets, before continuing to secure our main HQ/Compound"\
     ""\
     "<b>Defensive Fires:</b>"\
     "No known threat at this time."\
     ""\
     "<b>Airthreat:</b>"\
     "Mi-24s and Mi-8s"\
     ""\
     "<b>Morale:</b>"\
     "Very High."\
     ""\
     "<b>CBRN Threat:</b>"\
     "The enemy pose no CBRN Threat."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{F68E17261AD93D97}" {
     m_iOrder 2
     m_sTitle "A. Enemy Forces:"
     m_sContent "<h2>A. Enemy Forces:</h2>"\
     "<b>Equipment:</b>"\
     "CAF are equipped with their standard NATO weaponry, M16A1s series, LAWs/M67s, M249s, M60, FIM92 Stingers. etc"\
     "Wearing woodland coloured camo uniforms & helmets."\
     ""\
     "<b>Known Strength:</b>"\
     "1x Rifle Company (++)"\
     ""\
     "<b>Location:</b>"\
     "1x Rifle Platoon (+) is located on the West side of the Island of Skalisty"\
     "1x Rifle Platoon (+) is located on the North side of the Island of Skalisty"\
     "2x Rifle Platoons (+) is located on the Center of the Island of Skalisty"\
     ""\
     "<b>Capabilities:</b>"\
     "Access to FIM92 Stingers, LAWs"\
     "Vehicles include LAVII & HMMWVs"\
     "Captured ZU-23s"\
     ""\
     "<b>MLCOA:</b>"\
     "Ambush us as we land on the island, before pulling back."\
     ""\
     "<b>MDCOA:</b>"\
     "Ambush us as we land on the island, before pulling back, utilizing their stingers to deny us our air superiority."\
     ""\
     "<b>Defensive Fires:</b>"\
     "No known threat at this time."\
     ""\
     "<b>Airthreat:</b>"\
     "None."\
     ""\
     "<b>Morale:</b>"\
     "High."\
     ""\
     "<b>CBRN Threat:</b>"\
     "The enemy pose no CBRN Threat."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{E2A8FB01DADB2B19}" {
     m_iOrder 3
     m_sTitle "B. Friendly Forces:"
     m_sContent "<h2>B. Friendly Forces</h2>"\
     "<b>a. Disposition:</b>"\
     "Our Company is located on the island, we got 1x Platoon North & 1x Platoon West. (They will spawn when OPFOR draws near, AI Cached)"\
     ""\
     "<b>b. Higher Units Mission:</b>"\
     "Battalion has been assigned to support the US forces securing and \"Liberating\" this island from the Soviet Union."\
     ""\
     "<b>c. Composition:</b>"\
     "1x Platoon (-)"\
     ""\
     "<b>d. Strength:</b>"\
     "1st Platton - At 12x Man Strength"\
     ""\
     "<b>e. Supporting Fires:</b>"\
     "None."\
     ""\
     "<b>f. Attachments/Detachments:</b>"\
     "None."\
     ""\
     "<b>g. Additional Ammunition</b>"\
     "FIM Stingers"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{9113C6D4EC0078FE}" {
     m_iOrder 4
     m_sTitle "B. Friendly Forces:"
     m_sContent "<h2>B. Friendly Forces</h2>"\
     "<b>a. Disposition:</b>"\
     "All VDV Forces (YOU) are located at the Ugoldar military base as marked on the map"\
     ""\
     "<b>b. Higher Units Mission:</b>"\
     "Company has been tasked with securing the island of Skalisty"\
     ""\
     "<b>c. Composition:</b>"\
     "1x VDV Company (-)"\
     "1x Flight of Mi-24s"\
     "2x Flights of Mi-8s"\
     ""\
     "<b>d. Strength:</b>"\
     "340 - At 48x Man Strength."\
     "Stavok - At 4x Man Strength"\
     "Zakuska- At 8x Man Strength"\
     ""\
     "<b>e. Supporting Fires:</b>"\
     "None."\
     ""\
     "<b>f. Attachments/Detachments:</b>"\
     "2x Mi-24s"\
     "-- 8x Infantry Capacity Per Mi-24"\
     "4x Mi-8s"\
     "-- 16x Infantry Capacity Per Mi-8s"\
     ""\
     "<b>g. Additional Ammunition</b>"\
     "None."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{CD3FDA89FB02B72C}" {
     m_iOrder 5
     m_sTitle "II. Mission (Must Read):"
     m_sContent "<h2>II: Mission</h2>"\
     "Prevent the loss of the Western and/or Northern HQ.. if either of them are lost to the enemy, fall back to the main HQ/Compound before holding out until reinforcements arrive."\
     ""\
     "6x Respawns at start, if we lose North OR West, there will be a RESPAWN WAVE lasting 30sec, once over there will be no further respawns. "\
     ""\
     "4x FIM-Stingers will spawn at spawn in a crate in the middle of the road, when VDV Helicopters are within 3km from the main HQ"\
     "We do have a captured ZSU-23-2 Ural truck"\
     ""\
     "Adjacent Units (AI) will spawn upon the arrival of VDV Forces."\
     ""\
     "<b>Mission Maker Intent:</b>"\
     "- Mission COs or any leader will NOT order people out solo or by themselves, there must ALWAYS be a buddy team together if sent out. "\
     "- IF your team/squad gets wiped and/or you are alone, you will at the BEST of your abilities fall back to last known friendly forces and make contact VERBALLY before regrouping / rejoining another team/squad"\
     "- Focus Mi-24s first, once both are down you're free reign on Mi-8s"\
     "-- Exception, if Mi-8 are engaging you with PKM, you're clear to kill it."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{204FEF88E479B497}" {
     m_iOrder 6
     m_sTitle "II. Mission (Must Read):"
     m_sContent "<h2>II: Mission</h2>"\
     "(Not a Hard AO Limit for OPFOR/VDV)"\
     ""\
     "Secure the island of Skalisty, by securing first either West or North enemy HQ, and then afterwards secure the main enemy COY HQ at the center."\
     ""\
     "Each PLT HQ secured, gives us 40x more reinforcements at spawn to be airlifted to the AO. (We start at 30x Respawns)"\
     ""\
     "<h2>LOAD ORDER</h2>"\
     "- Zakuska 1"\
     "-- 341 PLT HQ"\
     "-- 341 Squad"\
     ""\
     "- Zakuska 2"\
     "-- 342 Squad"\
     "-- 343 Squad"\
     ""\
     "- Zakuska 3"\
     "-- 344 PLT HQ"\
     "-- 344 Squad"\
     ""\
     "- Zakuska 4"\
     "-- 345 Squad"\
     "-- 346 Squad"\
     ""\
     "- Company HQ chooses their bird, Zakuskas or Stavoks"\
     ""\
     ""\
     "Read Mission Notes."\
     "Intent is to secure the exterior HQs before securing the main COY HQ"\
     ""\
     "<b>Mission Maker Intent:</b>"\
     "- Mission COs or any leader will NOT order people out solo or by themselves, there must ALWAYS be a buddy team together if sent out. "\
     "- IF your team/squad gets wiped and/or you are alone, you will at the BEST of your abilities fall back to last known friendly forces and make contact VERBALLY before regrouping / rejoining another team/squad"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{CD7B612A2DA4CE08}" {
     m_iOrder 7
     m_sTitle "III. Execution:"
     m_sContent "<h2>III: Execution</h2>"\
     "<b>Intent:</b>"\
     "Protect our West and North PLT HQ, if either of them get lost to the enemy, we have to pull back to our main compound to hold out."\
     ""\
     "<b>1. Concept of the Operation:</b>"\
     "Platoon Commander's Discretion."\
     "It is advised to utilize our fellow comrades (AI) to locate the enemy and hit them before we have to pull back.. Also to shoot down the Mi-24s"\
     ""\
     "<b>2. Maneuver</b>"\
     "Platoon Commander's Discretion."\
     "It is advised to not split up the squads too much or too far ahead so they can mutually support one another if needed."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{6D1498FFD4F905E4}" {
     m_iOrder 8
     m_sTitle "III. Execution:"
     m_sContent "<h2>III: Execution</h2>"\
     "<b>Intent:</b>"\
     "Air assault onto Skalisty and secure the enemy HQs"\
     ""\
     "2x Mi-24s"\
     "-- 8x Infantry Capacity Per Mi-24 (16x Total)"\
     ""\
     "4x Mi-8s"\
     "-- 16x Infantry Capacity per Mi-8s (64x Total)"\
     ""\
     "<b>1. Concept of the Operation:</b>"\
     "Company Commander's Discretion."\
     "It is adviced to use the infantry to scout for any hard-to-attack locations and relay the information to the aircrafts which should only serve as direct firesupport to the main VDV Element"\
     ""\
     "<b>2. Maneuver</b>"\
     "Company Commander's Discretion."\
     "It is adviced to airassault onto either ONE of the external HQ locations as a singular force to maintain force composition before moving onto the main HQ itself."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{350CA60742AEAC96}" {
     m_iOrder 9
     m_sTitle "IV. Sustainment:"
     m_sContent "<h2>IV: Sustainment</h2>"\
     "<b>a. SOP Variations</b>"\
     "Dress: Standard Canadian Uniform"\
     "Equipment: Standard Canadian Loadout"\
     ""\
     "<b>b. Logistical Support:</b>"\
     "Replen Plan: None for 24h."\
     "Ammunition: Each man carries his own ammunition."\
     "IPE: Helmets and body armour are to be worn at all times."\
     ""\
     "Crate outside contains:"\
     "- 4x FIM92 Stingers"\
     "- 500x Sandbags"\
     ""\
     "<b>c. Medical:</b>"\
     "Location: Company Aid Post is to be setup by platoon medic."\
     "CASEVAC: By foot or with Platoon Assets like HMMWVs"\
     "Plan: Set up a casualty collection point and extract casualties to this point."\
     "Stretchers: None"\
     "Med Packs: Platoon medpack carried by platoon medic."\
     "Morphine: Every soldier carries 1+ stick of morphine."\
     ""\
     "<b>d. Vehicles:</b>"\
     "2x HMMWV M2s"\
     "2x HMMWVs"\
     "1x Captured ZSU-23-2 Ural"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{549F344E5E554E73}" {
     m_iOrder 10
     m_sTitle "IV. Sustainment:"
     m_sContent "<h2>IV: Sustainment</h2>"\
     "<b>a. SOP Variations</b>"\
     "Dress: Standard Soviet Uniform"\
     "Equipment: Standard Soviet Loadout"\
     ""\
     "<b>b. Logistical Support:</b>"\
     "Replen Plan: Replen for Helicopters, Ammo in helicopters."\
     "Ammunition: Each man carries his own ammunition."\
     "IPE: Helmets and body armour are to be worn at all times."\
     ""\
     "There are TWO helipads"\
     "1x Helipad with Mi-8s that ONLY Repairs and Refuels"\
     "Unlimited Repairs/Refuels"\
     ""\
     "1x Helipad with Mi-24 that Repairs, Refuels and Rearms"\
     "Has 2 400 Supplies to be used to rearm the Mi-24s, recommend using Mi-8's Helipad to repair/refuel"\
     ""\
     "Supply Cost for each Weapon Ammo;"\
     "- 12.7x108mm YakB | 100x rnd = 25x Supplies | 375x For Full Rearm"\
     "- UPK-23 23x115mm | 10x rnd = 6x Supplies | 300x For Full Rearm"\
     "- S8-KO 80mm Rockets | 1x rnd = 20x Supplies | 800x For Full Rearm"\
     "- 9M120 ATAKA ATGM | 1x Rocket = 100 Supplies | 400x For Full Rearm "\
     "- FLARES | 1x Flare = 1x Supplies | 128x For Full Rearm"\
     ""\
     "Full Rearm - 1 643 Supplies"\
     ""\
     "<b>c. Medical:</b>"\
     "Location: Company Aid Post is to be setup by platoon medic."\
     "CASEVAC: By foot or with company asset like Mi-8 or even Mi-24"\
     "Plan: Set up a casualty collection point and extract casualties to this point."\
     "Stretchers: None"\
     "Med Packs: Platoon medpack carried by platoon medic."\
     "Morphine: Every soldier carries 1+ stick of morphine."\
     ""\
     "<b>d. Vehicles:</b>"\
     "2x Mi-24s"\
     "- 1470x 12.7x108mm YakB"\
     "- 500x UPK-23"\
     "- 40x 80mm HEDP S-8KO"\
     "- 4x 9M120 ATAKA ATGM"\
     ""\
     "4x Mi-8s"\
     "- 2x PKMs"\
     "Mi-8 also carries:"\
     "- 30x Rnd of RPK Mags"\
     "- 100x Rnd of AK Mags"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{86640C41E74033C4}" {
     m_iOrder 11
     m_sTitle "V. Command & Signals:"
     m_sContent "<b>I. Chain of Command:</b>"\
     "21 Alpha, 21 Bravo"\
     ""\
     "<b>II. Callsigns:</b>"\
     "1st Section ------------------- 21 Alpha"\
     "2nd Section ------------------ 21 Bravo"\
     ""\
     "<b>III. Frequencies:</b>"\
     "1st Platoon Net ------------ 48.00 MHz"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_CAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{9BF8632B42F777B7}" {
     m_iOrder 12
     m_sTitle "V. Command & Signals:"
     m_sContent "<b>I. Chain of Command:</b>"\
     "340 -> 341 (Radio) -> 344 (Radio) -> 341 -> 342 -> etc"\
     ""\
     "<b>II. Callsigns:</b>"\
     "Company HQ ------------------------------ 340 (Radio)"\
     "Forward Air Support Liaisons ----- KAMENKA"\
     ""\
     "1st Platoon HQ --------------------------- 341 (Radio)"\
     "1st Rifle Squad --------------------------- 341"\
     "2nd Rifle Squad -------------------------- 342"\
     "3rd Rifle Squad --------------------------- 343"\
     ""\
     "2nd Platoon HQ -------------------------- 344 (Radio)"\
     "1st Rifle Squad --------------------------- 344"\
     "2nd Rifle Squad -------------------------- 345"\
     "3rd Rifle Squad --------------------------- 346"\
     ""\
     "1st Mi-24 ------------------------------------ STAVOK 1"\
     "2nd Mi-24 ----------------------------------- STAVOK 2"\
     ""\
     "1st Mi-8 -------------------------------------- ZAKUSKA 1"\
     "2nd Mi-8 ------------------------------------- ZAKUSKA 2"\
     "3rd Mi-8 -------------------------------------- ZAKUSKA 3"\
     "4th Mi-8 -------------------------------------- ZAKUSKA 4"\
     ""\
     "<b>III. Frequencies:</b>"\
     "Company Net ------------------------------ 42.00 MHz"\
     "Air Net	 --------------------------------------- 43.00 MHz"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{87D89E6CC7BF9E72}" {
     m_iOrder 13
     m_sTitle "VII. Air Control Manual (FASL MUST READ)"
     m_sContent "<h2>Table of Contents:</h2>"\
     "<b>- Different Types</b>"\
     "<b>- Example Transmissions between JTAC & Aircraft pilots:</b>"\
     "<b>- Formats for Transmissions</b> "\
     "<b>- Legends / Brevity Codes</b> "\
     "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------"\
     ""\
     "<h2>1) Type 1 Control.</h2>"\
     "<b>Type 1 control</b> is used when the JTAC/FAC must visually acquire the attacking Aircraft and the Mark / Target for control of each individual attack prior to weapons release / launch."\
     ""\
     "<h2>(2) Type 2 Control.</h2>"\
     "<b>Type 2 control</b> is used when the JTAC/FAC must visually acquire the attacking Aircraft OR the Mark / Target for control of each individual attack prior to weapons release / launch."\
     ""\
     "<h2>(3) Type 3 Control.</h2>"\
     "<b>Type 3 control</b> is used when the JTAC/FAC requires the ability to provide clearance for multiple attacks within a single engagement subject to specific attack restrictions. Type 3 control does not require the JTAC to visually acquire the aircraft or the target"\
     "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Example 5-Line Brief Transmission:</h2> "\
     "<b>Deuce31 (JTAC):</b>"\
     "“Deuce 31, Broadsword 11, 5-line, Type 2 control, BOT, rockets and guns, my position is checkpoint 295 marked by IR strobe, northwest 200, single technical vehicle marked by IR SPARKLE, make all attacks over my right shoulder, left pull, keep all effects of fires west of MSR Clovis.”"\
     ""\
     "<b>Broadsword 11 (A/C):</b>"\
     "“Deuce 31 copies over your right shoulder, left pull, keep all effects of fires west of MSR Clovis, pushing.”"\
     ""\
     "<b>Deuce31 (JTAC):</b>"\
     "“Deuce 31, CONTINUE.”"\
     ""\
     "<b>Broadsword 11 (A/C):</b>"\
     "“Deuce 31 and flight, VISUAL, TALLY, IN.”"\
     ""\
     "<b>Deuce31 (JTAC):</b>"\
     "“Deuce 31 and flight, CLEARED HOT.”<"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Example Situation Update Transmission:</h2> "\
     "<b>Deuce31 (JTAC):</b>"\
     "“Deuce 31, Broadsword 11, Friendlies are two companies in the vicinity of OP 2, one on the high ground and the other in a blocking position to the east. I am with the company on the high ground. There is also a Recon team at the northwest tip of Black Mountain, arty is firecapped at Firebase 5E, firing generally west, Break.”"\
     ""\
     "“Current surface-to-air threat is a SA-6 at KJ 123 456, just west of MSR Tampa; target is light armored company attempting to flank us to the north and two companies dug in three klicks to our west, Over.”"\
     "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Format: Rotary-Wing Close Air Support 5-Line Brief</h2> "\
     "Do not transmit line numbers. Units of measure are standard unless briefed. Restrictions are mandatory readback (*). JTAC may request additional readback. "\
     ""\
     "- 1. Observer/Warning Order"\
     "“(Aircraft Call Sign) _____________ , "\
     "This Is (JTAC Call Sign) _____________ , Over\" "\
     "5-line, Type (1, 2, or 3) C, MOA (BOC or BOT), (Ordnance Requested)"\
     ""\
     "- 2. Friendly Location/Mark "\
     "\"My position_____________ (TRP, Grid, etc.) , "\
     "Marked by _____________ (VS-17, Beacon, IR Strobe, etc.)\""\
     ""\
     "- 3. Target location "\
     "\"Target location, _________________________\" "\
     "(Bearing [magnetic] and Range [meters], TRP, Grid, etc.) "\
     ""\
     "- 4. Target Description/Mark"\
     "\" _____________ (Target Description) ,"\
     "marked by _____________ (IR sparkle, Tracer, etc.)\""\
     ""\
     "- 5. Remarks/Restrictions "\
     "*Final Attack Headings (FAHs) LTL/PTL "\
     "Surface-to-air threat"\
     "*Danger Close and initials"\
     "Additional calls requested"\
     "Additional remarks (GTL, weather, hazards, friendly mark)"\
     "*TOT/TTT "\
     ""\
     "The RW CAS 5-line should be passed as one transmission. If the restrictions portion is lengthy, it may be a separate transmission. "\
     "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Format: Situation Update (Controller to Close Air Support Aircraft)</h2>"\
     "<b>Situation Update # ____________________________ (if applicable) </b>"\
     "- Friendly Situation (disposition / posture, locations)"\
     "- Threat Activity (surface-to-air threats observed: who, what, when, where)"\
     "- Target – General Enemy Situation (“SALUTE” format – size, activity, location, uniform, time, equipment)"\
     "- Clearance Authority (Who has final control?)"\
     "- Ordnance Requested"\
     "- Restrictions"\
     "- Hazards (weather, terrain, obstructions)"\
     "- Remarks (JTAC capabilities, to include TLE if appropriate)"\
     ""\
     "Note: - This briefing should be broad in scope and will not be used as a substitute for a 5-line"\
     "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Legends / Brevity Codes</h2>"\
     "<b>- VISUAL</b> = Sighting of a friendly aircraft/ground position. Opposite of BLIND."\
     ""\
     "<b>- BLIND</b> = No visual contact of friendly aircraft/ground position. Opposite of VISUAL."\
     ""\
     "<b>- NO JOY</b> = Aircrew does not have visual contact with the target / bandit / landmark. Opposite of TALLY."\
     ""\
     "<b>- TALLY</b> = Sighting of a target, non-friendly aircraft, landmark, or enemy position. Opposite of NO JOY."\
     ""\
     "<b>- BOT</b> = Bomb On Target"\
     ""\
     "<b>- TOT</b> = Time On Target"\
     ""\
     "<b>- TTT</b> = Time To Target"\
     ""\
     "<b>- SEAD</b> = Suppression of Enemy Air Defenses"\
     ""\
     "<b>- ABORT</b>= Directive call to cease action/attack/event/mission. Do not release ordnance."\
     ""\
     "<b>- CLEARED HOT</b>=  Ordnance release is authorized in Type 1 or 2 terminal attack controls. "\
     ""\
     "<b>- CLEARED TO ENGAGE</b>=  JTAC Type 3 control clearance. Attack aircraft flight leaders may initiate attacks within the parameters imposed by the JTAC. Attack platforms will provide a “Commencing Engagement” call prior to engaging targets and an “Engagement Complete” call to JTAC, indicating completion of ordnance release."\
     ""\
     "<b>- CONTINUE</b>=  Continue present maneuver. Does not imply a change in clearance to engage or expend ordnance."\
     ""\
     "<b>- CONTINUE DRY</b>=  Continue present maneuver, ordnance release not authorized. Used to provide approval to aircraft to continue the pass without expending ordnance during Type 1, 2, or 3* controls. (*JTAC must use “Type 3, Continue Dry” for dry Type 3 controls.)"\
     ""\
     "Note: - This briefing should be broad in scope and will not be used as a substitute for a 5-line"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{9621CB20CAEC5438}" {
     m_iOrder 14
     m_sTitle "VI. Mission Notes:"
     m_sContent "<h2>VI. Mission Notes</h2>"\
     "<b>Timelimit:</b>"\
     "60m (Can be increased by GM's Discretion)"\
     ""\
     "<b>Mission Maker Intent:</b>"\
     "- Mission COs or any leader will NOT order people out solo or by themselves, there must ALWAYS be a buddy team together if sent out. "\
     "- IF your team/squad gets wiped and/or you are alone, you will at the BEST of your abilities fall back to last known friendly forces and make contact VERBALLY before regrouping / rejoining another team/squad"\
     ""\
     "<b>Canadian Army Victory:</b>"\
     "- by killing 90% of USSR (Incl. Respawns) or Timelimit is reached"\
     ""\
     "<b>VDV Forces Victory:</b>"\
     "by Capturing either; "\
     "-- West & COY HQ"\
     "-- North & COY HQ"\
     "-- West, North & COY HQ"\
     ""\
     "<b>Respawn:</b>"\
     "- OPFOR Gets 30x Respawn at start"\
     "-- Gets 40x Respawn for North HQ"\
     "-- Gets 40x Respawn for West HQ"\
     ""\
     "- BLUFOR gets 6x Respawn at start"\
     "-- Gets a Respawn Wave once either West or North HQ is lost."\
     "-- Only gets 1x Respawn Wave Total."\
     ""\
     "- If a pilot gets shot down.. "\
     "-- Congratulations, you're now following the ground infantry in"\
     "-- OR jump into a Mi-8 and be their gunner."\
     ""\
     "<b>GM Discretion as usual.</b>"\
     ""
    }
    GC_Briefing "{2F1D97EAB432B05F}" {
     m_iOrder 15
     m_sTitle "Game Mastering"
     m_sContent "<h2>Game Mastering:</h2>"\
     "This mission is not designed for game mastering and should only be manipulated for technical, administrative or diagnostic purposes."
    }
   }
  }
 }
